From 0aa5ced4edc7eb276153f16141180a14d02b9869 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:10:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] autotests: A surface that follows its depth is told the
 element limit

testElementLimit: since version 7 of kde_stereo_content_v1 a surface that
follows its depth hears the person's element limit (element_limit, pixels
of a view 1920 wide), 1 by default, before output_width and depth_limits,
again when the person changes it, unchanged when only the desktop's limits
change, and 0 when the person lays the elements flat. The test client keeps
the order of the group's events.

The test's init() checks the manager's version against the protocol's, 7;
it still expected 5 after version 6, so every function of the test failed
at init (queue row 910).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 autotests/integration/kwin_wayland_test.h     |  7 +++
 .../stereo_depth_exchange_test.cpp            | 46 ++++++++++++++++++-
 autotests/integration/test_helpers.cpp        | 15 ++++++
 3 files changed, 67 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

